{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm","id":1500723,"title":"What do you believe is the most underdeveloped part of VTM?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-19T05:54:37-08:00","id":1500723,"title":"What do you believe is the most underdeveloped part of VTM?","content":"IMO, it would have to be blood magic. I know a lot of people harp about how blood magic is too OP, but honestly, a lot of the paths are pretty boring and seem quite situational.<br /> <br /> The pre-revised version of Biothaumathurgy where you could alter life forms, even supernatural ones, was somewhat interesting. Something else that was unique about it was that you weren't just fleshing crafting them, but altering how they functioned, they're makeup, their nature, and their instincts. In the revised form it seems that the writers decided to turn it into more of a Frankenstein path where you animated dead things. It is depressing how they took something so interesting and turned it into something so boring. They could have at least combined the paths as a few users commented.<br /> <br /> What about you?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 01-19-2023, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T06:42:50-08:00","id":1500724,"title":"","content":"The part of VtM that I feel is the most underdeveloped would have to be the design of vampire society itself.<br /> <br /> If you look at the clans, bloodlines, blood magic, disciplines, hunter types, etc. all of them have been updated or retrofitted over time. But the core of vampire society hasn't been updated since the release of the Sabbat and Independents as playable factions and thus giving an option other than Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I am referring to the notion that any vampire run city is always a melting pot of multiple vampire clans, beyond the power structure of the say the prince and primogen there isn't a functional governing body, every vampire is supposedly utterly isolated while being under the rule of others, every vampire city is supposedly surrounded at all times by lupines that will shred any vampire who tries to leave but they never functionally invade and the vampires never create a defense against them. The list keeps going on and on, but suffice it say that most of vampire society design has never been revisited despite some massive plot holes it creates.<br /> <br /> I feel that each vampire held city should be more unique with its own customs and laws based on which clan controls the city, rather than factional alliance. For instance if you had a city that was controlled by Nagaraja, rather than having each vampire hunting on their own, it would make more sense to have public feeding system like the monsters have in <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0805570/?ref_=nv_sr_srsg_0\" target=\"_blank\">Midnight Meat Train</a>. This would have a very different feel to say a Toreador run city where creating the most prestigious Herds would be a form of status one upmanship. A Ventrue run city would probably have a central blood bank where every vampire is a member and you essentially have a subscription service for the blood types that you require or just enjoy.<br /> <br /> I understand the desire to make a generic template so that an ST can slap together a kindred political structure with little effort, but I feel it is way past due that the game update to give people the tools to construct vampire cities and societies in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T09:53:58-08:00","id":1500739,"title":"","content":"Well its been proactively un-developed (?) in v5 so this is a difficult question. For classic vtm id say lupine conflicts arnt explored and the ashirra needed a lot more fleshing out.<br /> <br /> biothaumaturgy was just life sphere so was intrinsically uninteresting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T12:34:10-08:00","id":1500759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1500739#post1500739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well its been proactively un-developed (?) in v5 so this is a difficult question. For classic vtm id say lupine conflicts arnt explored and the ashirra needed a lot more fleshing out.<br /> <br /> biothaumaturgy was just life sphere so was intrinsically uninteresting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldnt exactly say that its the life sphere. It does have a few similar powers, but then again we could say the same for many of the other vtm powers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T13:32:25-08:00","id":1500767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1500759#post1500759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldnt exactly say that its the life sphere. It does have a few similar powers, but then again we could say the same for many of the other vtm powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not quite the same but its very very close. Not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T14:11:22-08:00","id":1500770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1500739#post1500739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well its been proactively un-developed (?) in v5 so this is a difficult question. For classic vtm id say lupine conflicts arnt explored and the ashirra needed a lot more fleshing out.<br /> <br /> biothaumaturgy was just life sphere so was intrinsically uninteresting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with the Ashirra not being fleshed out and it would have been a great addition, I must point out that Veil of Night was a great book that should've been expanded/updated for the modern nights.<br /> <br /> I'll add the Tlacique from South America. That was an interesting concept that got introduced in World of Darkness 2nd ed and was being teased on many books across Revised edition. Their description on Blood Sacrifice was a fair introduction to them but so much was left out for a more proper use. I completely dislike their replacement by the Drowned Legacies, it's pointless to have those &quot;clans&quot;, or whatever they are, when life in South America is quite european-like in the big cities, especially with big names like Gratiano and Alexandra/Callisti y Callisto ruling over them.<br /> <br /> Another underdeveloped concept was the Hindi vampiric society. It started with Clanbook Ravnos revised and expanded a bit more on Blood Sacrifice. They've been expanded a little bit more through the V20 Dark Ages line but I think that their society structure was quite interesting to leave it as it was.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T20:48:32-08:00","id":1500807,"title":"","content":"Mostly settings. Like India really needed fleshing out. There's lots of different Vampire clans there, plus for centuries it was the primary intersection of Cainites and Wan Kuei. You also had other major non-vampire groups that made India their primary homeland (the Nagah from Werewolf and the Euthanatos from Mage). I really wish it had gotten properly explored back before 5th edition released and start changing and retconning material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T04:40:24-08:00","id":1500830,"title":"","content":"I actually really like the Cam as a global and multicultural organization and feel the ashirra would be obsolete/have largely outlived their purposes. Meanwhile India/Africa being their own thing reeks of exceptionalism/ a middle class urge to reject modernity and put on a pedastool societies perceived as more spiritual/primitive, even when they're not really that different and are intertwined with colonial history. &quot;Ventrue in India are magic users&quot; is fucking <i>asinine </i>and &quot;Ravnos in India are the Norm&quot; is really not a nice statement.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for what I think is undeveloped?<br /> Vampire physiology. All their fluids are blood? Stretching my faith in the masquerade a little too much there.<br /> <br /> Emotion manipulating Powers like Entrance and the blood bond are really, really too dependent on the mind of the storyteller and that can be quite a pain. <br /> <br /> I think we've trapped ourselves far too much into notions that a camarilla city needs primogen, and haven't put much consideration into how the Cam works with clans outside the Camarilla. Yes, it's easy to imagine it when you have some experience, but a lot of people are missing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T08:13:29-08:00","id":1500840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm#post1500723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, it would have to be blood magic. I know a lot of people harp about how blood magic is too OP, but honestly, a lot of the paths are pretty boring and seem quite situational.<br /> (...)<br /> What about you?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>There could certainly be more distinct paragraphs and definite information in regard to how Vampires establish themselves on a nightly basis in regard to securing standard / stable / perfect material conditions, wealth, access to basic and more complex data and information, and various good and interesting kinds of enjoyment, pleasure, and entertainment.<br /> <br /> I would say that these parts / aspects of Vampire: the Masquerade are rather often described in a way that can end up being superficial or incomplete.<br /> <br /> The various details, rules, laws, standards, and facts in regard to planning, logistics, philosophy, and cooperation (Both between individual Kindred and also as well the different most common or well-known groups and organizations of Vampires, Revenants, and Ghouls.) could definitely be more acutely and nicely narrated and described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-20-2023, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T06:04:41-08:00","id":1500922,"title":"","content":"For me that would be: Backgrounds and politics, power-struggles, social maneuvers and inner-sect dynamics. Also... Clan structure having use.<br /> <br /> -Backgrounds really are a very interesting idea, that very few games do in such a gradual way, generally making it a fixed Advantage or perk. Not something that can go up and down, have multiple forms, etc. But the game hardly uses it, never expands it, the ruleset is barebones. Elder and Ancilla games would be all about it, and getting to exploit, exchange it and have it on boon-trading. At the very least, Mind's Eye Theatre books give really good parameters, as well as Status uses, and hierarchy dynamics. I really don't know why, the tabletop game never did anything similar. Some sandbox games could really benefit from it; as it is, it feels as fluff for the character more than anything. The limits and uses for Backgrounds are way too abstract most of the time. V5 did some good on it, but not nearly enough.<br /> <br /> -Every sect feels homogenous in some aspect. Funnily enough, Sabbat, that would be the 'fanatical one-minded religious cultists', has it all. It has the Clan-identity and tradition, fighting against the antitribu no-clan mentality. It has inner factions, which is excellent, it's inspiring, and simple; loyalists, orthodox, moderates... all struggling to have their ideology and agenda advanced while juggling the material/practical needs in the city, and their self-identity and Clan. And of course, it has Paths of Enlightenment. As much as I like the more focused, less deep, and more pungent way the Sabbat is in V5, such a depth is welcome in a sect. Camarilla should be at the very least a bit factionalized, although it could be a lot more. The Requiem experience is really fun for intrigue and political-party wrangling in game, it gives a good baseline for more politicking in game. Anarchs would certainly have many 'ways to Anarch', be it more Baron-based, more commune, more true anarchy.... <br /> <br /> -While playing games, reading chronicles, and books... I hardly see all the deep and fun lore on Clans and their inner-workings mattering. Amicti Noctis? Doesn't matter. Ephorate? Can't see it. Tremere Pyramid? Don't think so. Gangrel things and Brujah raves? Never been in one. Maybe the problem is that as the common game has every player being a different Clan, a Storyteller would be hardly at fault to not make a customized exclusive list of events and grouping of 4-6 different Clans in a city, for every player. Which would also mean to read a lot of specific material. And trying to make it all relevant to the Chronicle too. So yeah, you read the clanbooks, lore of the clans, wikis, libellus sanguinis, and all that... but no official chronicle uses it. Maybe we should have more CLan-chronicles, like the Ventrue. Just to at least have a story in which such material has use. It seems like a waste of Clan culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T14:14:38-08:00","id":1500962,"title":"","content":"The most undeveloped part in VTM is definitely the Middle-East. That location should've been the most important part of the entire gameline, considering the West Asia was where the first cities began. Beyond 'Jerusalem by Night', I can't think of any part of Middle-East that has been expanded upon at all. And with V5 practically being another gameline within itself, we'll never see any official material about the Middle-East in VTM at all. Maybe some Storyteller Vault stuff, but nothing real to the game at all.<br /> <br /> Also another annoying undeveloped fact about VTM, is the fact very important Metaplot characters (that actually matter to the setting) like the Antediluvians (beside Tzimisce.. and he's not statted very well) are rarely given stats. Some may go along the lines of &quot;Antediluvians aren't meant to be statted, they're only mean to be plotpoints&quot;, but that notion is utterly ridiculous when VtM is supposed to be a tabletop game; not a book series (which unfortunately many people see oWoD as, instead of an experience to be played). <br /> <br /> Tremere definitely should have stats, considering how important he is in the setting, AND with how active he is; but he doesn't. Set should DEFINITELY have a stat sheet, considering how important he is to multiple oWoD gameslines.. but he doesn't..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T06:07:18-08:00","id":1501027,"title":"","content":"I will have to agree that making the metaplot, backstory etc. of the setting play a part in actual games is something which is underdeveloped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T13:25:50-08:00","id":1501050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1500922#post1500922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me that would be: Backgrounds and politics, power-struggles, social maneuvers and inner-sect dynamics. Also... Clan structure having use.<br /> <br /> -Backgrounds really are a very interesting idea, that very few games do in such a gradual way, generally making it a fixed Advantage or perk. Not something that can go up and down, have multiple forms, etc. But the game hardly uses it, never expands it, the ruleset is barebones. Elder and Ancilla games would be all about it, and getting to exploit, exchange it and have it on boon-trading. At the very least, Mind's Eye Theatre books give really good parameters, as well as Status uses, and hierarchy dynamics. I really don't know why, the tabletop game never did anything similar. Some sandbox games could really benefit from it; as it is, it feels as fluff for the character more than anything. The limits and uses for Backgrounds are way too abstract most of the time. V5 did some good on it, but not nearly enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Backgrounds need more substance, I would love it. But every time I try to mess with that it tends to break the game and setting quite thoroughly. The game setting and the themes just don't support those bigger ambitions.<br /> <br /> Resources alone shows how much the game doesn't really work with Backgrounds. Having lets say $1,000,000 in a bank account is a nice little chunk of change regardless of where you are in the USA.<br /> <br /> If you live in a backwoods area with minimal needs, you can buy an expansive plot of land, get a custom designed house built for all your vampiric needs, and still have money left in the bank for other things for years or maybe even decades to come. So relative score of Resources 4+.<br /> <br /> If you live in many places in California, the price of a three bedroom, two bath cracker box house with no upgrades and not being in the best part of town can easily run you close $650,000 to $750,000, though did see one go for $850,000 during the height of the price bubble. This leaves you with little money to spend on things and only a few years' worth of taxes and utilities before you are broke. So a relative score of Resources 3 or so.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you travel outside of the country and take that money with you, then you rank at about Resources 5+ in any third world economy.<br /> <br /> When you combine economic power with vampiric lifespan, privately owned cities become a thing that isn't really that unrealistic. The lore supports this concept that all the Elders own everything, but there never seems to be a connection between the lore and the PCs doing the exact same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T22:56:17-08:00","id":1501109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1500724#post1500724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am referring to the notion that any vampire run city is always a melting pot of multiple vampire clans, beyond the power structure of the say the prince and primogen there isn't a functional governing body, every vampire is supposedly utterly isolated while being under the rule of others, every vampire city is supposedly surrounded at all times by lupines that will shred any vampire who tries to leave but they never functionally invade and the vampires never create a defense against them. The list keeps going on and on, but suffice it say that most of vampire society design has never been revisited despite some massive plot holes it creates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah in comparison to something like &quot;Blade&quot; or &quot;Underworld&quot; the VTM Vampires seem kind of organized.<br /> <br /> If the Camarilla was really that powerfull I would expect them to have organized ways to get blood (like blood banks).<br /> <br /> <br /> I find also the equipment part of Vampire kind of laking. There are no special weapons to fight each other or other kinds of supernaturals. Or just things in general that make your unlife more safe and convenient.<br /> And the few things that exist are all Blood Magic, so most characters have no way of getting them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T23:46:40-08:00","id":1501120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501109#post1501109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah in comparison to something like &quot;Blade&quot; or &quot;Underworld&quot; the VTM Vampires seem kind of organized.<br /> <br /> If the Camarilla was really that powerfull I would expect them to have organized ways to get blood (like blood banks).<br /> <br /> <br /> I find also the equipment part of Vampire kind of laking. There are no special weapons to fight each other or other kinds of supernaturals. Or just things in general that make your unlife more safe and convenient.<br /> And the few things that exist are all Blood Magic, so most characters have no way of getting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly I believe the main issue is that if we made the adjustments, the game would turn into something else.<br /> <br /> Realistically speaking, a modern vampire would prioritize a secure haven and a live in Herd above politics or factions. Once technology hit the conference call stage, things like Elysium are not just outdated, but outright hazards because every hunter or alternate faction will hunt you there.<br /> <br /> Vampire society would be less Lost Boys fighting for survival on the street corners, and more bunch of shut-ins meeting online to socialize. The interesting thing is that with this setup, when two vampires go to war with each other, it would all be covert operations or recruiting clueless mortal pawns rather rolling through a city with a coterie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T03:23:23-08:00","id":1501125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501120#post1501120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realistically speaking, a modern vampire would prioritize a secure haven and a live in Herd above politics or factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if possible bagged blood would even preferable over a herd.<br /> I'm not sure about the V5 rules, but in the previous editions you needed iirc a pretty large Herd if wanted to be able to spend at least a few blood points each day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501120#post1501120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting thing is that with this setup, when two vampires go to war with each other, it would all be covert operations or recruiting clueless mortal pawns rather rolling through a city with a coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>That anyway a thing that never really worked imo in the official Setting.<br /> <br /> I remember the Berlin By Night Setting book where you had two princes at war each controlling one half of the city. Just that none of the two had remotly the man power to acually secure their part of the city, not even speaking about actually going to War...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T05:38:19-08:00","id":1501131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501050#post1501050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On the other hand if you travel outside of the country and take that money with you, then you rank at about Resources 5+ in any third world economy.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not strictly true. German money might afford you considerable advantages in obtaining land or labour in Brazil but a good chunk of the more premium items are going to be equally if not more expensive to acquire there. International brands like Apple or Ferari aren't going to discount their products just because most of the market can't afford them and the logistical difficulties/ fact that they're just catering towards elites is going to drive prices up. Even more modest international brands tend to be pricier in less developed areas, and don't you forget that the world's most expensive internet is found in the poorest countries. We should also consider the hidden costs, like poorer countries tending to be more overt in their corruption and the authorities may just find faults with a rich foreigner for easy financial gains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 01-23-2023, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T13:02:51-08:00","id":1501161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501125#post1501125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if possible bagged blood would even preferable over a herd.<br /> I'm not sure about the V5 rules, but in the previous editions you needed iirc a pretty large Herd if wanted to be able to spend at least a few blood points each day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Herd is one of those Backgrounds that can be very powerful or useless depending on which aspects you focus on and how you play your character. Using V20 for the purposes of discussion.<br /> Herd: * is 3 Vessels, which is enough to ensure basic survival from night to night.<br /> Herd: ** is 7 Vessels, which lets you spend a few blood points per night on top of basic feeding.<br /> Herd: *** is 15 Vessels, which pretty much covers a high BP use character build.<br /> Herd: **** is 30 Vessels, which covers a whole coterie of efficient users.<br /> Herd: ***** is 60 Vessels, which covers a whole coterie of high BP uses characters.<br /> <br /> Then you can pool the background for larger groups or higher use situations.<br /> <br /> A Tremere who specializes in Auspex and being a Seer who has a Gargoyle bodyguard can easily get away with a one or two dot Herd easily. But a Tremere who is constantly casting Thaumaturgy and doing Rituals by themselves should have a three or four dot Herd on hand. Given the proclivity for Tremere Chantries to be besieged, it really is a wierd plot hole for them not to maintain live in Herds of considerable size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T13:15:09-08:00","id":1501162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501131#post1501131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not strictly true. German money might afford you considerable advantages in obtaining land or labour in Brazil but a good chunk of the more premium items are going to be equally if not more expensive to acquire there. International brands like Apple or Ferari aren't going to discount their products just because most of the market can't afford them and the logistical difficulties/ fact that they're just catering towards elites is going to drive prices up. Even more modest international brands tend to be pricier in less developed areas, and don't you forget that the world's most expensive internet is found in the poorest countries. We should also consider the hidden costs, like poorer countries tending to be more overt in their corruption and the authorities may just find faults with a rich foreigner for easy financial gains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Many online apps and video games get region locked prices, despite there being no real supply chain issue.<br /> <br /> As for price gouging the elites, yes this is a thing, except in many the countries where you would be going to get more out of your money, the corruption or lax law enforcement is prevalent enough that the price gouger can end up brutalized or dead for the behavior. When transported to the WoD setting, this means it is even more cutthroat.<br /> <br /> Of course, in my opinion, if you are flaunting enough wealth that people will try to price gouge you, then you don't have enough experience with business. Even more so if you don't get a feel for the pricing before approaching a potential seller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T22:21:34-08:00","id":1501212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501161#post1501161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you can pool the background for larger groups or higher use situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is imo not great idea because if you pool you end up with an even larger number of vessels for the same amount of blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501161#post1501161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Tremere who specializes in Auspex and being a Seer who has a Gargoyle bodyguard can easily get away with a one or two dot Herd easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Gargoyle would also need about two points of Herd by him self.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501161#post1501161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Tremere who is constantly casting Thaumaturgy and doing Rituals by themselves should have a three or four dot Herd on hand. Given the proclivity for Tremere Chantries to be besieged, it really is a wierd plot hole for them not to maintain live in Herds of considerable size.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's say you have Chantrie with 5 Tremere and one Gargoyle, with 2-4 dots of herd for each of them that would be between 42 and 180 vessels. That would not be exactly easy to hide and to sustain.<br /> <br /> And if you really want to use you disciplines frequently with a character or play a combat or action heavy game (or even just combat or action heavy session once in a while) 5 Bloodpoints a day is also not that much. And even if you just have some Ghouls you need additional blood to feed them.<br /> <br /> Realistically I think with the rules for blood as they were in V20 and older, a pretty high priority for each vampire to find an inconspicuous\u200b way to get a large amount of blood regularly (and without wasting much time for hunting), and build up a pretty large storage for emergencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 01-24-2023, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T22:27:31-08:00","id":1501213,"title":"","content":"The Tremere should be heavily involved in the circulatory system and other blood-trade, since they are mainly lab-geeks who go through a lot of blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T00:36:37-08:00","id":1501220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501212#post1501212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Gargoyle would also need about two points of Herd by him self.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Not necessarily so, Auspex doesn't use BP for anything, so a Seer Tremere build is remarkably blood efficient in play style. This leaves the Gargoyle as the main blood consumer. A Herd score of two dots could feed both with a little left over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501212#post1501212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say you have Chantrie with 5 Tremere and one Gargoyle, with 2-4 dots of herd for each of them that would be between 42 and 180 vessels. That would not be exactly easy to hide and to sustain.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those situations where real world situations make the WoD default setup nonsensical. A while back there was a discussion on the forums about doing things like renovating a decommissioned missile silo for a vampire haven. The average sale price for such a silo and surrounding land is about $300,000 which is cheaper than most three bedroom houses these days. When turned into a survival bunker, such silos can house 75+ people for up to five years without a supply run.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't take much to retrofit such an apocalypse bunker into one hell of a Tremere chantry with full live in Herd for each vampire. 13 ton blast doors that are nuclear blast resistant mixed with Thaumaturgy warding and ghoul security..... makes you really wonder why the Tremere would ever bother making a Chantry in a city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T04:36:28-08:00","id":1501229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501220#post1501220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily so, Auspex doesn't use BP for anything, so a Seer Tremere build is remarkably blood efficient in play style. This leaves the Gargoyle as the main blood consumer. A Herd score of two dots could feed both with a little left over.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are forgetting that you need 1 BP every night just to rise. Meaning that you need at 2 points of Herd if you want at least occasionally spend for something else.<br /> <br /> And if we are going away from that example, if you have a combat vampire (especially one with Celerity) or a one who practices Thaumaturgy or another for of Blood Magic, and want to actually train the use of your powers you can easily burn through BP in the double digits.<br /> <br /> So I think ways to get large amounts of Blood regularly, without going on killing sprees or having to keep large numbers of vessels around, is really something that is missing from the rules.<br /> <br /> Btw. it would already help if the number of vessels would grow linearly with the Background/the number of Blood Points you get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 01-24-2023, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T17:59:21-08:00","id":1501289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501229#post1501229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are forgetting that you need 1 BP every night just to rise. Meaning that you need at 2 points of Herd if you want at least occasionally spend for something else.<br /> <br /> And if we are going away from that example, if you have a combat vampire (especially one with Celerity) or a one who practices Thaumaturgy or another for of Blood Magic, and want to actually train the use of your powers you can easily burn through BP in the double digits.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire loses 1 BP per night for waking, one dot in Herd gets you three Vessels, it takes about 48 hours for a Vessel to regenerate enough to be fed on again. By feeding on the Herd in turn, by the time you have cycled through the Herd, the first is able to be fed on again. Thus 7 vessels at Herd two is enough for a couple of vampires.<br /> <br /> I agree that some vampire builds are absurdly BP expensive. But at the same time, probably due to the groups I have played with, I see those very expensive builds as being lower tier choices compared to more BP efficient builds. A game with minimal combat focus means the Blood economy is completely different from a combat focused game. Conversely if you are playing an indirect combat game, the blood economy gets even weirder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T06:47:10-08:00","id":1501316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501289#post1501289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A vampire loses 1 BP per night for waking, one dot in Herd gets you three Vessels, it takes about 48 hours for a Vessel to regenerate enough to be fed on again. By feeding on the Herd in turn, by the time you have cycled through the Herd, the first is able to be fed on again. Thus 7 vessels at Herd two is enough for a couple of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh we mostly played Dark Age:Vampire, where you get just one BP per Night per Point of Background and the number of Vessels is just Fluff, I never realised that this is different in V20...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T07:59:57-08:00","id":1501317,"title":"","content":"This is one of those situations where real world situations make the WoD default setup nonsensical [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <br /> To be fair that's every rpg. If you ever put legitimate thought and planning into the situation it's usually fairly easy to nullify whatever conflict the setting relies on. Presumably the explanation in wod is they've already all been taken by reclusive vampires as soon as their abandoned and up for sale. Entirely to just wait out the apocalypse<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27701-psychotobe","name":"Psychotobe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T12:33:48-08:00","id":1501336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501316#post1501316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh we mostly played Dark Age:Vampire, where you get just one BP per Night per Point of Background and the number of Vessels is just Fluff, I never realised that this is different in V20...</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that should be another thing to put on the list of underdeveloped aspects, the fact that the systems are not consistent across settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T12:45:49-08:00","id":1501337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psychotobe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501317#post1501317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair that's every rpg. If you ever put legitimate thought and planning into the situation it's usually fairly easy to nullify whatever conflict the setting relies on. Presumably the explanation in wod is they've already all been taken by reclusive vampires as soon as their abandoned and up for sale. Entirely to just wait out the apocalypse</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I have always been a fan of exploiting the aspect of gaming where a little bit of planning or thought nullifies aspects of the game.<br /> <br /> If you play a fighter, there are mechanics to represent how good a fighter you are. If you want to play a magic caster, then there is a list of spells and rituals to learn and use. If you play a &quot;thinking&quot; character on the other hand, there are rarely mechanics to support it.<br /> <br /> It's kind of like trying to play a genius inventor like Edison or Tesla, who are defined by their ability to redefine the technology of the setting but are inherently not allowed to change the setting or its mechanics. So you instead just role play a person with whacky ideas that never really do anything in the long run.<br /> <br /> We get a vicarious thrill from the thought of being able to be the action hero and do ridiculous amounts of violence in games, mostly due to the mechanics being designed to allow us to experience it. But how do mechanically support the thrill of being the smartest person in the room? Few games get within a mile of mechanically supporting a &quot;<a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/XanatosGambit\" target=\"_blank\">Xanatos Gambit</a>&quot; style character that isn't an NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T18:03:11-08:00","id":1501766,"title":"","content":"Geographically, probably the Indian subcontinent and its vampire population. <br /> <br /> More generally, what vampires do for entertainment, which gets into issues of Elysium, the Rack, and other parts of the game which weren't fleshed out as much as they could've been. <br /> <br /> What happens when vampires have the Fame background, how this impacts their standing in Kindred and mortal society, all the Masquerade issues which crop up, issues of feeding/Herds, Resources, fame vs infamy, and so on. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T02:08:34-08:00","id":1501790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501337#post1501337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you play a fighter, there are mechanics to represent how good a fighter you are. If you want to play a magic caster, then there is a list of spells and rituals to learn and use. If you play a &quot;thinking&quot; character on the other hand, there are rarely mechanics to support it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mental Attributes are in general kid of underused, outside of Blood Magic and Auspex there are hardly any discipline powers that need where you roll any checks with mental attributes (except for some pretty exoctic ones like Temporis or Mytheratica).<br /> <br /> Meaning that with most clans being smart makes you pretty bad at your clan disciplines...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T04:18:04-08:00","id":1501799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501766#post1501766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geographically, probably the Indian subcontinent and its vampire population.</div> </div> </div> </div>[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Explain why you think this could and should be different. Because Mystic Ventrue/respected Ravnos reeks of racist insinuation. Like other than The Tremere maybe having more competition and the Ventrue replacing their hardon for the Roman empire with something more local there's nothing that really needs to change beyond what hats people wear. Indian Settites might famously play different instruments but they're playing the same tune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T04:47:26-08:00","id":1501803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501790#post1501790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mental Attributes are in general kid of underused, outside of Blood Magic and Auspex there are hardly any discipline powers that need where you roll any checks with mental attributes (except for some pretty exoctic ones like Temporis or Mytheratica).<br /> <br /> Meaning that with most clans being smart makes you pretty bad at your clan disciplines...</div> </div> </div> </div>A depressing blind spot in game design to be sure.<br /> <br /> There was a bit of fluff in one supplement (Gilded Cage?) about how a camarilla vampire defeated an entire sabbat pack that illustrates the problem. In the story, the sabbat pack was using Earth Meld to sleep in an empty dirt lot in the city they were attacking, once the camarilla vampire figured out where they were he arranged to have the lot turned into a parking area, having it paved over in one day. The sabbat are stuck there until someone digs them up, and camarilla vampire gets additional income due to the paid parking.<br /> <br /> Mechanically that is little more than using a few Backgrounds (Contacts * / Influence * / Resources *** or ****) to completely negate the combined stats of the entire sabbat pack. The mental attributes don't really factor into the choices made beyond not being so low as to call into question the ability to conceive of such a plan.<br /> <br /> I have dealt with several STs who felt that such a plan is anticlimactic and ruins the effort put into designing the NPCs. So even if mechanically it is a sound idea, the books don't really make a case for it being acceptable in general.<br /> <br /> Combine a Background heavy character build with access to Animalism, Auspex, Dominate, Presence, Thaumaturgy, or Necromancy and you have a character that never sets foot on the battlefield personally but can defeat high quality combat builds. I guess a better way to put it would be how does a professional boxer fight a hacker if the boxer doesn't know who the hacker is and has no clue where they are, and this is assuming the Boxer knows that a hacker is targeting them in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T06:48:42-08:00","id":1501809,"title":"","content":"Not using it for disciplines =/= not useful. If anything not needing to use disciplines is seen as a strength in Vampire society, using disciplines often means you've screwed up somewhere, and stuff rarely used in games like intelligence is great for accumulating and maintaining backgrounds and although you can get around this with a smart retainer/ally or two that can go very wrong so personal intelligence is best. It is unfortunate that many ST's have a bias against players coming up with really clever solutions that allow them to circumvent challenges, and I've personally felt a lot of frustration when my plans to fix problems and get rewards without showing up have been ruined by contrivances because the ST wanted me to heroically duke it out with a Sabbat pack... but this is an ST problem, not a game problem.<br /> <br /> And wits/perception are God-Stats that every character should put a lot of points in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T12:50:18-08:00","id":1501828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501809#post1501809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is unfortunate that many ST's have a bias against players coming up with really clever solutions that allow them to circumvent challenges, and I've personally felt a lot of frustration when my plans to fix problems and get rewards without showing up have been ruined by contrivances because the ST wanted me to heroically duke it out with a Sabbat pack... but this is an ST problem, not a game problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it as a game problem because it is the books fluff and mechanics which inform the ST &amp; Players what is possible. The lack of support for indirect combat or combat advantage negation is a consistent feature across most if not all of the WoD game lines. Exalted tried to create social combat system, but only made a social combat system for face to face interactions and dropped the ball on indirect combat Background based options.<br /> <br /> Its kind of like having an old west stand off where a swordsman, a gunfighter, and a brawler are all threatening to get into a fight with each other, but the last player asks if they can plant a bomb in the area the night before or use a sniper rifle from almost a mile away. Yes there are rules for explosives and guns, but very little page space being given to that style of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T05:02:43-08:00","id":1501864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501809#post1501809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And wits/perception are God-Stats that every character should put a lot of points in.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Int is often times not that use full.<br /> <br /> Btw. the problem with the Disciplines also exists for Knowledge Abilities. Appart from Occult and (far less frequent) Medicine non are used. For most Clans putting Mental and Knowledge primary is going to make you really terrible at using your disciplines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T08:12:35-08:00","id":1501870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501766#post1501766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More generally, what vampires do for entertainment, which gets into issues of Elysium, the Rack, and other parts of the game which weren't fleshed out as much as they could've been.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to be noted that Vampires (and also Ghouls and Revenants) can choose to have fun and partake in the spectrum and range of available hobbies, interests, crafts, social evens, and entartainment that is simply and normally available. The events, media, culture, and activites can be adjuted and modified to a smaller or greater degree, up to and past the point of resembling what could be called usual or mundane.<br /> <br /> In regard to curious events, fun activities and interesting entartainment that is specific to groups, cultures, religions, and organisations of the Kindred, there are clearly social saloons, chess clubs (And maybe other board games are included, as well. Also - Vampires from Clan Ventrue have the Chessmaster faction / group / organisation.), riddle contests, and scavengers or treasure hunts, and of course art and cultured focused events, concerts, meetings, and performances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T08:55:28-08:00","id":1501872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501864#post1501864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Int is often times not that use full.<br /> <br /> Btw. the problem with the Disciplines also exists for Knowledge Abilities. Appart from Occult and (far less frequent) Medicine non are used. For most Clans putting Mental and Knowledge primary is going to make you really terrible at using your disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Int is difficult because it's almost impossible to portray someone smarter than yourself, and frustrating to play someone dumber. Should you refrain from using that clever tactical idea you had because your character's Intelligence is 1 or 2, and in real life you are a 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T11:03:08-08:00","id":1501882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501864#post1501864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Int is often times not that use full.<br /> <br /> Btw. the problem with the Disciplines also exists for Knowledge Abilities. Appart from Occult and (far less frequent) Medicine non are used. For most Clans putting Mental and Knowledge primary is going to make you really terrible at using your disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>This depends entirely on your characters, storyteller, and what you want from the game. If you're really only using Occult and medicine, you're probably towards the territory of an Autuark in an 80's action flick. If you actually want to be respected in a camarilla game, things like academics and politics are necessary if your ST cares about you making real allies and establishing yourself as respectable and more than a disposable grunt to be lead around by the nose, and Law can be very essential if your ST is a bit of a bastard. (also, knowledges changes maybe the most between 1e and 20th so... yeah)<br /> <br /> Perhaps their's room to encourage the use of knowledges for more but I don't think they're needed for more disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T19:25:48-08:00","id":1501913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501872#post1501872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Int is difficult because it's almost impossible to portray someone smarter than yourself, and frustrating to play someone dumber. Should you refrain from using that clever tactical idea you had because your character's Intelligence is 1 or 2, and in real life you are a 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the nightmare scenario where the ST IRL is an Int 2 or 3 and they have players with IRL higher scores.<br /> <br /> STs practically have to be &quot;renaissance men&quot; with an incredibly varied knowledge base to deal with &quot;thinking characters&quot;. There was one group I played with where the ST duty would rotate. One ST had relatively little computer knowledge in real life and as such trying to be a hacker was incredibly difficult and usually ineffectual in their games. A different ST in the same group had a job in network design and computer security.... mortal hackers in those games could defeat whole coteries, let alone what a nosferatu schrecknet user or a tremere with path of technomancy do to enemy coteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T19:31:34-08:00","id":1501914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501882#post1501882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps their's room to encourage the use of knowledges for more but I don't think they're needed for more disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the problem is that Intelligence or Knowledge is a catch all term, but what it references is very specific. Brawl covers all hand to hand, be it boxing, wrestling, or martial arts, but functionally there is no difference between them on how you damage another character. Knowledge of history doesn't give you the ability to perform surgery, nor does being highly intelligent give you access to knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T01:00:40-08:00","id":1501937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501914#post1501914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of the problem is that Intelligence or Knowledge is a catch all term, but what it references is very specific. Brawl covers all hand to hand, be it boxing, wrestling, or martial arts, but functionally there is no difference between them on how you damage another character. Knowledge of history doesn't give you the ability to perform surgery, nor does being highly intelligent give you access to knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Academics is very explicit that it doesn't cover hard science, just as Athletics is very explicit that it doesn't cover brawl, melee, dancing or horseriding. <br /> <br /> I find with knowledges it's very effective to go wide and compensate with a bunch of intelligence. It's a strategy that will make you utterly ineffectual in V5 due to how the dice work there, but fortunately I'm not playing V5.<br /> <br /> <br /> As most vampires enjoy conversation and like to see themselves as refined not having Academics is likely to lead to embarrassment in polite society. Kindred are going to look down on you and they're petty enough that you might make enemies or embarrass your sire when you ask them to explain what they mean from some commonly known reference. Academics can be a great help in giving you a conversation topic with someone like the prince, or at least steer you away from bad conversation topics. <br /> <br /> Brawl... like performance, there's some important commonalities between different disciplines. Wrestlers and kickboxers might have completely different ways of inflicting their bodies on others but their is a lot of comonalities for these skills: distance, predicting movement, timing, balance, using compound rather than simple movements... etc. Academics likewise gives you History, geography, sociology, psychology... and helps you sort BS from likely truth. <br /> <br /> Politics is really important for vampires. working out who to toady up to, who to side with, how to avoid purges, what would happen if X went missing... <br /> <br /> IDK, some knowledges are odd. Things like technology or computers are like.. why are they seperate skills? Some things like science really are only useful for a few character concepts (IE making drugs or bombs or magic or making friends with that other kindred scientist) but I think you'd be wrong to suggest most primary knowledges aren't worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T21:08:34-08:00","id":1502006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501937#post1501937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Politics is really important for vampires. working out who to toady up to, who to side with, how to avoid purges, what would happen if X went missing...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those things that is also underdeveloped in VtM. The default idea of an intricate society of Machiavellian interactions between apex predators. When in truth, based on the population ratios RAW, there are like six vampires in a large city and that is assuming max vampiric population in those ratios.<br /> <br /> So it is less political infighting and more a few people down at the pub arguing over the football game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T06:52:44-08:00","id":1502305,"title":"","content":"I want to be cheeky and say the Anarchs. <br /> <br /> What makes them different from the Camarilla and the Sabbat at the same time ? What's their groove to replace the Vampire Supremacists of the Sabbat (whom I always liked even if their ideas are horrible at best) ?<br /> <br /> What do Anarchs believe in, and how do they build something out of their beliefs ?<br /> <br /> So far, from what little I know of V5 (and even Mascarade) they seem to be Camarilla-lite without the Illuminati vibe, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T07:42:40-08:00","id":1502306,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs are one of the most pointless factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T13:43:29-08:00","id":1502322,"title":"","content":"Anarchs being undeveloped is the point. They vaguely believe in something, anything, that isn't in line with what the prince wants, which kind of means they believe in nothing and, like the Protestants who originally yearned to go back to basics and be free of excess traditions, the most prominent were ironically the ideologues. Anarchs are whatever the ST wants them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T13:52:13-08:00","id":1502323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1502322#post1502322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchs being undeveloped is the point. They vaguely believe in something, anything, that isn't in line with what the prince wants, which kind of means they believe in nothing and, like the Protestants who originally yearned to go back to basics and be free of excess traditions, the most prominent were ironically the ideologues. Anarchs are whatever the ST wants them to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It works in previous editions (kinda) were theyre defined as a dissident movement in carmarilla or holdout in sabbat territories but in v5 where they have numbers and territory it's a massive problem. Especially as the carmarilla doesn't lay claim to them, is weaker and doesnt even care a great deal about them and the sabbat barely exist so you're stuck with Rebel without a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-06-2023, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T14:18:51-08:00","id":1502325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1502323#post1502323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It works in previous editions (kinda) were theyre defined as a dissident movement in carmarilla or holdout in sabbat territories but in v5 where they have numbers and territory it's a massive problem. Especially as the carmarilla doesn't lay claim to them, have the clout it used to or even care a great deal and the sabbat barely exist so you're stuck with Rebel without a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>In V5, the Anarchs actively oppose the Camarilla and seek to replace them. I think that's the difference. That's the point of the rebellion in V5. Somehow Anarchs are still this grabbag of various beliefs and ideologies, though...<br /> <br /> With the old lore, Anarchs have always been to me more like a term defined by what they're not. As long as the Camarilla and the Sabbat are rejected, you're an Anarch. But that's about it. There's no actual &quot;faction&quot; with power here. Just an umbrella-term for various factions and ideologies that reject the other two factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T23:15:35-08:00","id":1502349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1502325#post1502325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In V5, the Anarchs actively oppose the Camarilla and seek to replace them. I think that's the difference. That's the point of the rebellion in V5. Somehow Anarchs are still this grabbag of various beliefs and ideologies, though...<br /> <br /> With the old lore, Anarchs have always been to me more like a term defined by what they're not. As long as the Camarilla and the Sabbat are rejected, you're an Anarch. But that's about it. There's no actual &quot;faction&quot; with power here. Just an umbrella-term for various factions and ideologies that reject the other two factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly but that's completely pointless since they don't really propose an alternative system and the replacing the carmarilla is redundant since it already surrendered the right to rule when it withdrew its claim of universal membership and that's before we consider the collapse of the Sabbat and population decline freeing up massive amounts of territory making it questionable if you even have to deal with the carmarilla.<br /> <br /> Yeah that was a problem back then and I'd argue its still a problem now. If anything I'd argue the anarchs have always been underwritten but v5 emphasises this problem further since the focus is on them. They worked better in Revised but even then their were issues.<br /> <br /> v5 really really needed to give the anarchs, defined ideological praxis and definitive contrasts with both the Sabbat and the carmarilla. Instead it stuck with &quot;I hate the prince because he's a jerk and he's got 600 years on me.&quot; And homeless chique vs conventional fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-07-2023, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T01:48:37-08:00","id":1502366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1501882#post1501882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This depends entirely on your characters, storyteller, and what you want from the game. If you're really only using Occult and medicine, you're probably towards the territory of an Autuark in an 80's action flick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm specifcally talking about the use in Disciplines in older Editions. Occult is used for Roles in many of the more Supernatural Disciplines (which are usually Clan Specific) and Medicin is used for Vicissitude, some Necromany Powers and maybe Obeah/Valeren I think. And that's it.<br /> <br /> In you have basically three types of Attributes/Abilities: Physical, Social and Mental. Based on how character creation works you can start usually good in one them, ok in anther and pretty weak in the third.<br /> <br /> The thing is with going with Physical or Social will usually give you some synergy with fitting Disciplines, Mental and Knowledges usually wont unless you go for a very specific Clan.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T02:35:49-08:00","id":1502369,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Occult&quot; is a very stupid knowledge insofar as it means &quot;Vague smattering of academics and/or streetwise related to myths and legends&quot; but also &quot;the very specific protoscientific combination of theurgy, alchemy, alternative medicine or astrology you use to perform miracles&quot; <br /> ...and so I think every branch of thaumaturgy should come with it's own specific knowledge rather than just relying on occult, and a lot of the reflexive occult rolls should be something else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is with going with Physical or Social will usually give you some synergy with fitting Disciplines, Mental and Knowledges usually wont unless you go for a very specific Clan. </div> </div> </div>I understand this completely, I just fail to see how this is a considerable issue. Given the same or even a somewhat smaller amount of points I can make a discipline-light character that can mop the floor with the overwhelming majority of discipline-optimized users. There's a few very specific abilities and creative methods that make this difficult but there's always caveats like that. <br /> <br /> Disciplines =/= power. Power=power. A character is by no means worse because they've got 4 politics rather than 4 melee. In a conflict, I would wager the former is going to live longer. Even as we get to social disciplines inhuman charm can frequently lose to very human wisdom and knowledge. Dominate and Presence isn't better than Money and Influence (and like, if they're both vampires, the knowledge one is still going to have some disciplines which probably lend themselves towards an advantage) <br /> <br /> Am I saying things are perfect? No. Talents are almost always primary over Skills and Knowledges and the whole 13/9/5 system has significant flaws. But I think you're a little too wrapped up in the idea of having super powers if you think knowledges aren't worth it because they're not used for Disciplines. I think your tunnel vision is pretty evident in how you view medicine. Medicine is the discipline that helps vampires avoid diseased blood and reduces the number of humanity rolls they need to make over their lifetime of forcing sharp things into people and siphoning their life force while also suppressing a violent Beast. Fleshcrafters using medicine is an ancedote for most vampires; keeping the body count down is important for everyone. Thinking the way you do is ok for stories, but it's not good for chronicles. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T05:54:33-08:00","id":1502382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1502349#post1502349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly but that's completely pointless since they don't really propose an alternative system and the replacing the carmarilla is redundant since it already surrendered the right to rule when it withdrew its claim of universal membership and that's before we consider the collapse of the Sabbat and population decline freeing up massive amounts of territory making it questionable if you even have to deal with the carmarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't the Camarilla already not recognize the Giovanni as members after refusing to help the Cappadocians?<br /> <br /> The Camarilla <i>claimed</i> all vampires were members but that's always been a fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T07:27:00-08:00","id":1502390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1502382#post1502382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't the Camarilla already not recognize the Giovanni as members after refusing to help the Cappadocians?<br /> <br /> The Camarilla <i>claimed</i> all vampires were members but that's always been a fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The exception kind of proves the rule. The carmarilla explicitly excluded the clan of death which had a tacit assumption you are automatically carmarilla. It was also a temporary realpolitik agreement with clauses.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its a de jour law, the carmarilla pre 5th took it very seriously partly because it provided a causus beli for conflict with other groups and justifies jurisdiction on Johnny anarch or john the diablerist ravnos. It wasn't universally enforced but that isn't for trying.<br /> <br /> Edit-it would have also been very useful in v5 as a key conflict point with the Anarchs since it gives them an automatic point of contention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-07-2023, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T22:06:15-08:00","id":1502480,"title":"","content":"In my opinion the most underdeveloped part of VtM has always been Backgrounds. I understand that the 1st edition was made in 1990 when all RPG's were mainly about combat, but I can't understand how 30 years later we still don't have a proper system to fight each other using resources, influence and allies as weapons, but we have an awful lot of fighting maneuvers. <br /> I have developed my own HB system for this, but I think many more things could be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T11:41:02-08:00","id":1502528,"title":"","content":"I would like to see other city settings myself. I enjoyed the Chicago By Night along with New York and the Cairo By Night books that I was able to find recently and in very good condition I might add as a further plus and got to see others elements and I'm will be buying more of the older books when I can to get a better feel for the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T00:57:02-08:00","id":1502592,"title":"","content":"We need a V20 Baghdad by Night book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T03:11:41-08:00","id":1502596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1502592#post1502592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a V20 Baghdad by Night book.</div> </div> </div> </div>We might get a Dark Ages book on Baghdad in the Storyteller's Vault later this year. Just saying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T11:37:15-08:00","id":1502619,"title":"","content":"Maybe they will do an updated version of Vancouver by Night and how the independent Prince there is handling everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T16:11:26-08:00","id":1503705,"title":"","content":"Anarchs should have been given the Factions treatment (all sects in fact) that Sabbat got. I still can't believe the original boogeyman, the fanatical diablerist vampires who despise humanity, and are bound by a mindwashing Vinculum, and live under a strict regimen of loyalty and violence, are the sect who gets the political spectrum, the different positions and ideologies. It is an awesome structure for character (player) political choice, because Sect is something that the gaming table decides and that's it. Besides small exceptions, you can't have a group with different sects, they are way too belligerent. Anarchs are very uninteresting in most editions, and yeah, V5 spotlight on them just showed the cracks and emptiness. <br /> <br /> There should be all kinds of Anarchs. They are mostly diluted in a general anarchy, that mostly goals for a dog eat dog world, without structure. In the end is almost like anarchocapitalism ideology. Cuz they aren't as collaborative as they perhaps should, and instead of critics (in-universe or otherwise) making thoughtful comments like &quot;yeah, Anarchs are hypocrites who only destroy things and take down Princes cuz of envy, and they don't build nothing in place&quot;, they are just telling a very obvious truth. The Anarch State in US sounds like a mess, with no plan. <br /> <br /> Maybe Anarchs should've been a great mass of different ideological groups, that unite themselves in opposition to Camarilla, and refusal of Sabbat. Both the ruthless Barons and the idealistic Freedom fighters are part of it, and should be in constant fighting. I would through the Prometheans in too, after all, they are much closer to building a new Carthage than a Camarilla domain is (ideally). The Anarchs don't got a theme anymore, and hell, in our current state of affairs and generation, they should be the most interesting and popular group among players. And have really good material. At least I think so. underdeveloped for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T19:42:17-08:00","id":1503723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503705#post1503705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchs should have been given the Factions treatment (all sects in fact) that Sabbat got. I still can't believe the original boogeyman, the fanatical diablerist vampires who despise humanity, and are bound by a mindwashing Vinculum, and live under a strict regimen of loyalty and violence, are the sect who gets the political spectrum, the different positions and ideologies. It is an awesome structure for character (player) political choice, because Sect is something that the gaming table decides and that's it. Besides small exceptions, you can't have a group with different sects, they are way too belligerent. Anarchs are very uninteresting in most editions, and yeah, V5 spotlight on them just showed the cracks and emptiness.<br /> <br /> There should be all kinds of Anarchs. They are mostly diluted in a general anarchy, that mostly goals for a dog eat dog world, without structure. In the end is almost like anarchocapitalism ideology. Cuz they aren't as collaborative as they perhaps should, and instead of critics (in-universe or otherwise) making thoughtful comments like &quot;yeah, Anarchs are hypocrites who only destroy things and take down Princes cuz of envy, and they don't build nothing in place&quot;, they are just telling a very obvious truth. The Anarch State in US sounds like a mess, with no plan.<br /> <br /> Maybe Anarchs should've been a great mass of different ideological groups, that unite themselves in opposition to Camarilla, and refusal of Sabbat. Both the ruthless Barons and the idealistic Freedom fighters are part of it, and should be in constant fighting. I would through the Prometheans in too, after all, they are much closer to building a new Carthage than a Camarilla domain is (ideally). The Anarchs don't got a theme anymore, and hell, in our current state of affairs and generation, they should be the most interesting and popular group among players. And have really good material. At least I think so. underdeveloped for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may not like this suggestion, but the Carthian Movement is basically the Requiem counterpart to the Anarchs. You could take their <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/11871/Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">faction book</a> and mine it for Anarch material. The book describes Humanists that emphasizes living among the herd, a survivalist militia called The Final Civilization, and Radical Collectivists, to show the faction's broad political spectrum. There's also some freakish groups like the Night Doctors, who do medical research on vampires and/or ghouls, and Hives, which are coteries so fanatically collectivist they dress, act, and think alike (almost like Blood Brothers).<br /> <br /> I'm <b>NOT</b> saying play Requiem. I am saying Requiem has exactly the kind of stuff you're asking for. Instead of waiting for an Anarch faction book from Onyx or Renegade to eventually come out, you could salvage one released years ago and make your broad spectrum of Anarch factions from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 02-22-2023, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T21:39:48-08:00","id":1503730,"title":"","content":"My biggest observation about anarchs is they don't actually have anything alternate proposed the system they typically operate under is ultimatly kratocracy so they'll end up back to DA eventually even if they win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T22:20:53-08:00","id":1503732,"title":"","content":"Perhaps they should go back to their feudalistic roots to flesh out the Anarchs? I've always viewed all three sects as the main three variations on feudalism throughout history:<br /> The Sabbat are the version of feudalism that mainly follows the will of the Pope, and goes on crusades in his name.<br /> The Camarilla is the version of feudalism where the High Nobles and Monarchs have most of the power.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are the version of feudalism where the Low Nobles have more collective power than the High Nobles and Monarchs. That's a pretty respectable chunk of the old timey world, by the way. The Roman &quot;Republic&quot; was really feudalism where the Low Nobles had more collective power than the High Nobles. Large chunks of Ancient Greece where times/places where the Low Nobles had more collective power than the High Nobles. Really, &quot;democracy&quot; for a long time just meant a situation where the low nobles had more collective power than the high nobles.<br /> <br /> So perhaps the Anarchs should create a Roman Republic/Ancient Greek &quot;democracy&quot; form of government.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T22:42:20-08:00","id":1503734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1502390#post1502390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exception kind of proves the rule. The carmarilla explicitly excluded the clan of death which had a tacit assumption you are automatically carmarilla. It was also a temporary realpolitik agreement with clauses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a difference between not having a representative on the Inner Circle and not being under the authority - in some fashion - of the Camarilla. The Giovanni were clearly never represented on the Inner Circle. Yet I would argue that whatever the arrangement of the Promise of 1528 was, it put them in some capacity under the Camarilla's authority even if it limited the ways the Camarilla could interfere with the clan. I always felt the early clan description as limiting them to three embraces per generation was obviously part of the agreement, and that there were more restrictions.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Treaty of Tyre clearly put the Assamites under some sort of governance/administration of the Camarilla even though that clan too was not part of the Inner Circle.<br /> <br /> Only the Ravnos and Setites didn't have clear governance. But the Ravnos originally seemed so decentralized that it would have been futile to try to do so, and after it was revealed the Setites had been offered membership in the Inner Circle, I always felt that there was some sort of informal arrangement or ongoing (if sporadic) negotiations that created some sort of deal even if the Setites would often violate it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T22:44:08-08:00","id":1503735,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat needs a political spectrum because it's rules, ideas and policies are incredibly complicated. <br /> The Camarilla is just &quot;guy with the most backing is in charge, he can make whatever rules he likes, but we all have this idea of a code we shouldn't break and there's a small international body that makes suggestions and sometimes hunts intercity criminals. <br /> The Anarchs are simply &quot;guy with most backing is in charge, but he's probably weaker so he can't do as much&quot; <br /> <br /> They're too simple to really need a spectrum, and that's by design too. A storyteller can make their prince tyranical or he can clearly be the voice of reason quelling the chaos of his constituents, or he can be a weak and powerless puppet, or we can have a council of elders that do everything without a prince. Anarchs can be Camarilla light, powerless vampires looking for equality, or reactionary fanatics wishing for religious freedom so they can practice some really inhumane paths in peace. They are loosely defined so they can be what the storyteller wants them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T02:41:08-08:00","id":1503745,"title":"","content":"Looking back, this is how the V5-corebook pitched the Anarch-movement:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The revolution against the Camarilla is as old as the sect itself. Originally known as the Anarch Revolt, in recent decades it has grown vastly, as younger Kindred find it hard to understand why they should follow the dictates of elders who seem perfectly happy to throw them to the Second Inquisition if need be.<br /> <br /> The unbound are all those vampires who fall outside the Camarilla. The Anarch Movement in its various forms is a subset of the unbound and also their most visible manifestation. Many seek to escape from the Camarilla\u2019s control by hiding. But the Anarchs have decided to fight back, attempting to conquer and control domains originally held by those who would claim themselves their masters. And why not? The Camarilla\u2019s elders are being called to the Middle East by the Beckoning, and the Second Inquisition has destroyed princes and primogen all over the world.<br /> <br /> The number of elders dwindle while there is a new crop of hungry, ambitious Anarch licks every year. The word on the street is revolution. No more compromises, no more politics, no more trying to make deals with the Camarilla. The Movement has finally escaped the centuries-long lethargy it fell into after the Convention of Thorns and the formation of the Sabbat, but that time is now over.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs have remembered how to fight, galvanized by the Camarilla\u2019s great betrayal in being at fault for the Second Inquisition.\u200b<br /> <br /> The Movement is different in each city. Sometimes an Anarch city has a ruler called a baron. More commonly, it is led by gangs who each have their own territories. Some cities are currently divided between the Anarchs and the Camarilla \u2013 both sides itching to take over.<br /> <br /> Where the Camarilla influences human society from the outside, the Anarchs have burrowed deep inside. Many maintain mortal identities, perhaps even families and jobs. This makes them simultaneously more vulnerable and more secure. Vulnerable because they are in contact with their surroundings every night, and sure to make mistakes. Secure because the Anarch is never the vampire lord in a mansion on the hill. They\u2019re the DJ in the nightclub, the terrifying cop from internal affairs, the junkie creeping outside your window.<br /> <br /> What motivates the Anarch Movement most of all is the scent of victory. For the first time in centuries, it feels as if it might be possible to topple the Princes. If the old order can collapse in Berlin, it can collapse anywhere!\u200b </div> </div> </div>Two things strucke me in that writeup: A lot hinges on the idea of the Beckoning and SI weakening Elders or making them disappear. And the second thing is that it just glosses over the idea that <i>somehow </i>unlike in the past the Anarchs in V5 aren't lethargic and are itching to seek conflict with the Camarilla and overthrow them. Although this very much needs explanation: How did the Anarchs even go from &quot;We're not the Camarilla.&quot; to &quot;We're against the Camarilla.&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T05:23:11-08:00","id":1503748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503745#post1503745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back, this is how the V5-corebook pitched the Anarch-movement:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Two things strucke me in that writeup: A lot hinges on the idea of the Beckoning and SI weakening Elders or making them disappear. And the second thing is that it just glosses over the idea that <i>somehow </i>unlike in the past the Anarchs in V5 aren't lethargic and are itching to seek conflict with the Camarilla and overthrow them. Although this very much needs explanation: How did the Anarchs even go from &quot;We're not the Camarilla.&quot; to &quot;We're against the Camarilla.&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> yeah its a major problem, the anarchs are still pretty much the same as previous editions with no meaningful changes except being more beligerant. if anything conflict is decentivised due to population drop. Theirs no elders to fight and plenty of turf to go around, plus any actual conflict is a terrible idea with the 2nd inq ongoing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T07:19:28-08:00","id":1503752,"title":"","content":"I'd theorize that the explanation lays with the Brujah.<br /> <br /> The Brujah left the Camarilla and, with the help of the Gangrel and the Ministry basically set the Anarchs up as a new, rival sect. They carry a grudge against the Ventrue and are using their new faction to smash up the Ventrue's faction because like, fuck Ventrue, I guess. The Brujah made up the majority of the Anarchs even before the clan officially left the Camarilla, and they probably continue to make up a majority of the sect, especially in leadership positions where they don't really have any rivals (the Gangrel generally aren't interested in leading and the Ministry typically pulls strings from behind the scenes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T07:44:21-08:00","id":1503753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503734#post1503734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there is a difference between not having a representative on the Inner Circle and not being under the authority - in some fashion - of the Camarilla. The Giovanni were clearly never represented on the Inner Circle. Yet I would argue that whatever the arrangement of the Promise of 1528 was, it put them in some capacity under the Camarilla's authority even if it limited the ways the Camarilla could interfere with the clan. I always felt the early clan description as limiting them to three embraces per generation was obviously part of the agreement, and that there were more restrictions.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Treaty of Tyre clearly put the Assamites under some sort of governance/administration of the Camarilla even though that clan too was not part of the Inner Circle.<br /> <br /> Only the Ravnos and Setites didn't have clear governance. But the Ravnos originally seemed so decentralized that it would have been futile to try to do so, and after it was revealed the Setites had been offered membership in the Inner Circle, I always felt that there was some sort of informal arrangement or ongoing (if sporadic) negotiations that created some sort of deal even if the Setites would often violate it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is important to remember that the purfiew, capabilities, influence, reputation, and resources of the Camarilla might be rather limited in regard to some categories, areas, groups, and organizations. Hence for example Autarkis Vampires and many Assamites or Setites might have been more or less outside reach of the Kindred focused on advancing the goals and priorities of the Camarilla. The events and occurances in regard to these factors could be different between eras or decades of course.<br /> <br /> I do wonder - whether the Indpendant Clans do have some sort of guaranteed and definite representation, friendliness, consideration, respect and optimism in regard to them on the Camarilla Inner Circle? Maybe it is that one or two Vampires who sit on this council are asked or requested to at least make some effort in this direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T10:44:07-08:00","id":1503762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503748#post1503748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah its a major problem, the anarchs are still pretty much the same as previous editions with no meaningful changes except being more beligerant. if anything conflict is decentivised due to population drop. Theirs no elders to fight and plenty of turf to go around, plus any actual conflict is a terrible idea with the 2nd inq ongoing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of feeds into a criticism I always had with the Beckoning as a plot device: why are you killing all the Elders offscreen, when the PCs should be doing that <i>in-game</i>? <br /> <br /> All it does is create a situation where Elders are thin on the ground, and the only ones you really have to fight...are other young Kindred. The intended axis of conflict - young versus old - is misaligned with what the practical effects of the metaplot change would be.<br /> <br /> And if the Elders are still strong enough to effect real control and influence in the setting, then functionally the Beckoning did nothing. If the youth are meant to fight the old, we didn't need a Beckoning for this. V5 could simply have presented the Anarchs becoming more belligerent and willing to fight Elders as the new status quo. A time of upheaval, that the PCs are <i>right in the middle of</i>. Not an upheaval that already happened and that the PCs need scramble to take advantage of.<br /> <br /> It also misses the point of the Punk theme. You're not the young taking the reigns of a power structure that was already ceded to you. You're the young throwing off the shackles of old, entrenched monsters clinging to wealth and control. It was the message Punk put forward back in the 80s and 90s, and a message very relevant today. &quot;The powerful will not give up their power willingly, and no outside force will make them. You have to take back the world yourself, together.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T12:53:03-08:00","id":1503769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503762#post1503762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sort of feeds into a criticism I always had with the Beckoning as a plot device: why are you killing all the Elders offscreen, when the PCs should be doing that <i>in-game</i>?<br /> <br /> All it does is create a situation where Elders are thin on the ground, and the only ones you really have to fight...are other young Kindred. The intended axis of conflict - young versus old - is misaligned with what the practical effects of the metaplot change would be.<br /> <br /> And if the Elders are still strong enough to effect real control and influence in the setting, then functionally the Beckoning did nothing. If the youth are meant to fight the old, we didn't need a Beckoning for this. V5 could simply have presented the Anarchs becoming more belligerent and willing to fight Elders as the new status quo. A time of upheaval, that the PCs are <i>right in the middle of</i>. Not an upheaval that already happened and that the PCs need scramble to take advantage of.<br /> <br /> It also misses the point of the Punk theme. You're not the young taking the reigns of a power structure that was already ceded to you. You're the young throwing off the shackles of old, entrenched monsters clinging to wealth and control. It was the message Punk put forward back in the 80s and 90s, and a message very relevant today. &quot;The powerful will not give up their power willingly, and no outside force will make them. You have to take back the world yourself, together.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrc, one of the developers said this edition is about replacing the old system with something new, and seeing if this new system is any better than the old. I'm paraphrasing massively as I don't remember the exact words, but that seemed to be the gist of it.<br /> <br /> Which is implies that defeating the few remaining elders is almost expected to be the cold open of this edition. Defeating the elders is like defeating Scarecrow in the second Bale Batman movie: something almost perfunctory before getting to the REAL story.<br /> <br /> And the real story is mostly you dealing with this almost post apocalyptic setting in which you are mostly hiding from the SI and random little gangs of rival Anarchs and Sabbat remnants, while dealing with you own dwindling humanity and doing soap-opera stuff with Touchstones, maybe killing your sire in hopes of becoming human again, and maybe trying to build a new system in this post-apocalyptic world, knowing this is doomed because of vampire nature.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Walking Dead&quot; stuff, combined with &quot;Santa Clarita Diet&quot; stuff, in other words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T12:53:04-08:00","id":1503770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503753#post1503753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is important to remember that the purfiew, capabilities, influence, reputation, and resources of the Camarilla might be rather limited in regard to some categories, areas, groups, and organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. At the end of the day, the Camarilla's resources are just the individual vampires who comprise the Jusitcars and Archons, plus whatever influence and other assets other vampires in the organization deign to provide to assist them. Enforcing their will on the Independents is limited as most of their time and efforts are simply concentrated on policing the domains nominally loyal to them and more important threats like the Sabbat. There are probably whole cities, regions, and affairs the Inner Circle never bother to do anything about not to mention independent domains like Vancouver (comprised primarily of vampires of the Camarilla clans) and sects and societies like the Inconnu and Children of Osiris.<br /> <br /> At the same time, at the local level most Princes and their entourage can put a lot of pressure on any independent member who shows up on their domain, as they'll be confidant that they have superior local resources and escalation dominance from support from the Justicars and Archons.<br /> <br /> My point was simply that the Camarilla does in fact regulate some of the Independent Clans to some degree, at least prior to Revised when things like the Treaty of Tyre and the Tremere curse were thrown out the window, and the Giovanni were portrayed as a much larger clan than originally intended (although this does have its origins in late 2e era with the first Giovanni Clanbook).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T14:50:57-08:00","id":1503777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503769#post1503769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Irrc, one of the developers said this edition is about replacing the old system with something new, and seeing if this new system is any better than the old. I'm paraphrasing massively as I don't remember the exact words, but that seemed to be the gist of it.<br /> <br /> Which is implies that defeating the few remaining elders is almost expected to be the cold open of this edition. Defeating the elders is like defeating Scarecrow in the second Bale Batman movie: something almost perfunctory before getting to the REAL story.<br /> <br /> And the real story is mostly you dealing with this almost post apocalyptic setting in which you are mostly hiding from the SI and random little gangs of rival Anarchs and Sabbat remnants, while dealing with you own dwindling humanity and doing soap-opera stuff with Touchstones, maybe killing your sire in hopes of becoming human again, and maybe trying to build a new system in this post-apocalyptic world, knowing this is doomed because of vampire nature.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Walking Dead&quot; stuff, combined with &quot;Santa Clarita Diet&quot; stuff, in other words.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue I always had with that approach is that if you wanna go down that route then the WOD has to be darker. Rather than Urban Fantasy, the focus should be on apocalyptic or post-apocalyptic storytelling-tropes. But the context for WOD-games is still supposed to be the present-day world we live in. And before Justin Achilli, the idea was that it was merely slightly worse (in addition to all sorts of supernatural horror being real).<br /> <br /> Not that you can't do it... but both V5 and W5 (in different ways) are hitting a wall when these ideas have to contend with the idea that the setting is still supposed to be the world we live in (sort-of).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T15:49:44-08:00","id":1503783,"title":"","content":"But it's not post-apocalyptic for the humans, just the vampires. Things are actually looking up for humans, since the age of monsters is finally ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T16:00:34-08:00","id":1503784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503783#post1503783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's not post-apocalyptic for the humans, just the vampires. Things are actually looking up for humans, since the age of monsters is finally ending.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a matter of world-building.<br /> <br /> But Beckoning and Second Inquisition aren't indicators or &quot;things looking good&quot;. At least, that isn't how it was presented. The Beckoning is an indication of a powerful supernatural force awakening and the Second Inquisition is an authoritarian extremist version of human hunters.<br /> <br /> And H5 is all about saying that the SI is an impediment to protecting humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T21:45:42-08:00","id":1503791,"title":"","content":"It being post apocalyptic is pretty awkward, ecologically its actually closer to the long night era of their history, except the environment is way better for them with urbanisation. If anything things are pretty good for the average neonate in terms of competion. The game has to effectively ignore its own set up to work since theirs so much turf up for grabs conflict becomes absurd. <br /> <br /> Your actual big problem in v5 is you're a twitchy screw up whose stuck in unhealthy relationships with your prey and your powers don't compensate enough for your flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-24-2023, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T22:03:52-08:00","id":1503792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503784#post1503784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And H5 is all about saying that the SI is an impediment to protecting humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is pretty funny because the SI has been an absolute tour de force in v5 while the street hunters don't achieve anything and probably can't inflict long term damage full stop. It's the technocracy issue all over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-24-2023, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T07:19:13-08:00","id":1503807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503791#post1503791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It being post apocalyptic is pretty awkward, ecologically its actually closer to the long night era of their history, except the environment is way better for them with urbanisation. If anything things are pretty good for the average neonate in terms of competion. The game has to effectively ignore its own set up to work since theirs so much turf up for grabs conflict becomes absurd.<br /> <br /> Your actual big problem in v5 is you're a twitchy screw up whose stuck in unhealthy relationships with your prey and your powers don't compensate enough for your flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the whole setup with the Beckoning and the Sabbat disappearing for their Gehenna War was always strange. Also, turning the entire Middle East into Mordor or something as part of that... Then again this cavalier attitude toward mixing present-day realities with these Kindred-specific setting elements is what gave us the V5-scandal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T07:24:06-08:00","id":1503809,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Those street hunters aren't going to be taking out the Tremere's Chantry in Vienna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T07:40:44-08:00","id":1503811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503809#post1503809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Those street hunters aren't going to be taking out the Tremere's Chantry in Vienna.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;But they're like the man, man. Working in cohesive groups and actual achievements is totally fash.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T08:10:37-08:00","id":1503813,"title":"","content":"Taking on the prime chantry should really be like the subject of a war film. Now whether that means piles of dead bodies and rivers of blood or simply organizing the planning and political shenanigans needed to have multiple strikes from high-yield ordinances shatter the place without undue attention is really up to preferences but in any case &quot;it was bombed&quot; doesn't suffice. V5 metaplot is woefully undeveloped as a general rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T08:41:13-08:00","id":1503817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503813#post1503813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking on the prime chantry should really be like the subject of a war film. Now whether that means piles of dead bodies and rivers of blood or simply organizing the planning and political shenanigans needed to have multiple strikes from high-yield ordinances shatter the place without undue attention is really up to preferences but in any case &quot;it was bombed&quot; doesn't suffice. V5 metaplot is woefully undeveloped as a general rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much any off the events prior to v5 should have been a massive plot arc. Theirs enough in their to cover an entire edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T09:32:28-08:00","id":1503819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503770#post1503770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was simply that the Camarilla does in fact regulate some of the Independent Clans to some degree, at least prior to Revised when things like the Treaty of Tyre and the Tremere curse were thrown out the window, and the Giovanni were portrayed as a much larger clan than originally intended (although this does have its origins in late 2e era with the first Giovanni Clanbook).</div> </div> </div> </div>Various interactions like diplomacy, lore trading, hostilities, spying, antagonisms, or information brokering might be done to a considerable and meaningful extent by Kindred from the Camarilla who are definitely experts and specialists in regard to a particular Clan or organisation - this includes having both knowledge and also the means to be involved with particular Vampires succesfully.<br /> <br /> It has to be noted that if matters become too serious or complex for these experts to deal with, they can very well ask for help and support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T18:39:04-08:00","id":1503871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503813#post1503813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking on the prime chantry should really be like the subject of a war film. Now whether that means piles of dead bodies and rivers of blood or simply organizing the planning and political shenanigans needed to have multiple strikes from high-yield ordinances shatter the place without undue attention is really up to preferences but in any case &quot;it was bombed&quot; doesn't suffice. V5 metaplot is woefully undeveloped as a general rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, remember in Mage's &quot;Horizon War&quot; trilogy, where three whole books were dedicated to the Ascension Warrior engineering the destruction of Doissetep?<br /> <br /> Because it seems like the destruction of Clan Tremere's Vienna chantry is important enough to justify at least one novel. Instead, it's a summary in a larger book, where it all happens offscreen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T12:15:56-08:00","id":1503911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503723#post1503723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may not like this suggestion, but the Carthian Movement is basically the Requiem counterpart to the Anarchs. You could take their <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/11871/Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">faction book</a> and mine it for Anarch material. The book describes Humanists that emphasizes living among the herd, a survivalist militia called The Final Civilization, and Radical Collectivists, to show the faction's broad political spectrum. There's also some freakish groups like the Night Doctors, who do medical research on vampires and/or ghouls, and Hives, which are coteries so fanatically collectivist they dress, act, and think alike (almost like Blood Brothers).<br /> <br /> I'm <b>NOT</b> saying play Requiem. I am saying Requiem has exactly the kind of stuff you're asking for. Instead of waiting for an Anarch faction book from Onyx or Renegade to eventually come out, you could salvage one released years ago and make your broad spectrum of Anarch factions from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth considering to mine other related settings to fill in gaps in your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T19:51:56-08:00","id":1503925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503723#post1503723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may not like this suggestion, but the Carthian Movement is basically the Requiem counterpart to the Anarchs. You could take their <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/11871/Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">faction book</a> and mine it for Anarch material. The book describes Humanists that emphasizes living among the herd, a survivalist militia called The Final Civilization, and Radical Collectivists, to show the faction's broad political spectrum. There's also some freakish groups like the Night Doctors, who do medical research on vampires and/or ghouls, and Hives, which are coteries so fanatically collectivist they dress, act, and think alike (almost like Blood Brothers).<br /> <br /> I'm <b>NOT</b> saying play Requiem. I am saying Requiem has exactly the kind of stuff you're asking for. Instead of waiting for an Anarch faction book from Onyx or Renegade to eventually come out, you could salvage one released years ago and make your broad spectrum of Anarch factions from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I'm all for it. Especially because I've already done so. I myself have factionalized every sect the game has, as to have an easier time painting the political map of the game, and in a city. It gives a good general direction for an NPC, and grounds for alliances and coups. And there is much Clan material or really deep buried in supplements that corroborate with these additions.<br /> <br /> But basically I took the Council of Scales (of which Critias is part of) idea and made it the moderate Promethean Anarch-sympathizer Camarilla group. Which envelops some Carthian (Cartagenian in this case) ideals. <br /> Many orders like the Bitter Ashes, Crooked Cross, Apostles of the Third Caine, Twilight Order... etc. were part of a Lancea Sanctum-like network of friendly groups/orders. Just like military and monk orders would get along. While the Church of Caine (Cainite Heresy) was an opposition to them. After the major sects formed, they kind of pulverised, keeping some old contacts, but either going Autarkis, Camarilla or Sabbat.<br /> And, I took the Ventrue hierarchy, that is a lot of material to keep entirely hidden in a Clan (and in-game, probably one player will interact with that), and made it so as to be more &quot;open&quot;. Its taking the idea of Salons from the book Elysium, and making a big club of elite inside the Camarilla, that already is a club of elite. Of course, after the Anarch War, there was a lot or rabble inside, and the High-Low Clan structure had just collapsed, so the High found a way to distinguish themselves. They are like the Invictus. A club dominated by Ventrue, and the most influential Camarilla Kindred, that in the most higher-ups, help decide who sits in the Inner Circle. And well, after the general meetings end, the non-Ventrue go, and the Clan sits pure Directorate style. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I really like how Requiem did politics, and stole a lot of it and mixed together in weird concoctions. The re-work I did on Anarchs is a bit more extensive, and falls out of the matter addressed in the thread.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-25T23:11:14-08:00","id":1503928,"title":"","content":"Making <b>Fall of London </b>the first chronicle in a series of book about the big upheavals of the V5 setting would be very cool. IDK if it would sell, but you could definitely make the case for a <b>Fall of Berlin </b>book further detailing what happened in the demo, a <b>Fall of Wien </b>blowing up the Great Chantry, a <b>Fall of Venice </b>with the birth of the Hecata, and a <b>Fall</b> <b>of</b> <b>Mexico</b> <b>City</b> with the Fourth Sabbat Civil War. Also, a <b>Fall of Montreal </b>connected to the CHAPTERS game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T10:24:12-08:00","id":1504124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1500723-what-do-you-believe-is-the-most-underdeveloped-part-of-vtm?p=1503928#post1503928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making <b>Fall of London </b>the first chronicle in a series of book about the big upheavals of the V5 setting would be very cool. IDK if it would sell, but you could definitely make the case for a <b>Fall of Berlin </b>book further detailing what happened in the demo, a <b>Fall of Wien </b>blowing up the Great Chantry, a <b>Fall of Venice </b>with the birth of the Hecata, and a <b>Fall</b> <b>of</b> <b>Mexico</b> <b>City</b> with the Fourth Sabbat Civil War. Also, a <b>Fall of Montreal </b>connected to the CHAPTERS game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a terrific idea, absolutely amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26110-ramon-nogueras","name":"Ramon Nogueras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}